      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠬᠠᠯᠢᠮ</unicode>
      <uighur>qalim</uighur>
      <cyrillic>халим</cyrillic>
      <transcript>XALIM</transcript>
      <definition>1 n. The fat and flesh adhering to the hide of an animal just skinned; a whole sheep skinned carefully in order to leave these tissues on the body of the animal (formerly offered as a gift to the bride's family to formalize an engagement).</definition>
